curret idea:
write batched mcts
then run it in paralell to get multithreaded perforance and better gpu utilization

options:
individual tree traversal, node holds one game
- simpler mcts code
- requires game rewrite for single game performance - well desn't strictly require it.

paralell tree exploration, nodes store stats indexed by zorbist hash or move path
- more complicated mcts
- potentially faster
- no game engine rewrite


on the same exact request, asking for methods to make single batch implementation faster,
sonnet: 5% -> 6%        1%
opus: 6% -> 8%          2%
fable: 8% -> 13%        5%


implement update cap on low probability with gamma





each node holds a game and node stats.

nodes are looked up by hashing instead of path.

so we start of with n nodes. each steps untill they reach a leaf, accumulate into one model call.

a node kinda needs to store a whole game becasue we need to be able to copy it to step to a new game. and we kinda need to store all games separately because otherwose how would separate nodes work?

however because game steps are so simple, and because we no longer lookup by path but by state, we could build a completelly standalone hashing method that runs lightning fast and allows for moves directly.